## BuildOrderData: the fixed build orders the TdAutotest bot plays (GDD §10.2).
## The bot runs the steps in order, each as soon as it is affordable (and not
## before its wave), so a build order plus a seed always gives the same run.
## Data only, no logic.
class_name BuildOrderData
extends RefCounted

## Order keys:
##   spells — true: the bot casts its spells and the ultimate (TdAutotest policy).
##   loadout — optional: the three spell ids brought in (default SpellData.DEFAULT_LOADOUT).
##   bonus_souls — optional, test orders only: souls granted at the start (earned
##             as "test_bonus") so one run can exercise every evolution.
##   ultimate — optional (gw2-kit): SpellData.ULTIMATES id brought (when --ultimate is not given).
##   steps_by_map — optional (gw2-kit): {map id: steps} in place of `steps`, so one
##             order (--build=kit_a / kit_b) plays on every map. A map's entry may be
##             {"base": order id, "swap": [from, to]} instead: that order's steps with
##             its first build of tower `from` building `to` (DECISIONS Y5).
##   steps  — step rows. Keys:
##     do    — "build" | "upgrade" | "evolve" | "target" | "sell".
##     spot  — "plot:N" or "post:N" (index into the map's plots / posts).
##     tower — TowerData id ("build" only).
##     mode  — TowerData.TARGET_MODES value ("target" only).
##     wave  — optional: not before this wave number has started (1-based; 0 = before wave 1).
